Upstream engine
---------------
scripts/ — the GeoInt recon pipeline (recon, intake, meta, ocr, textgeo,
prior, detect, calib, board, evidence, photo_session, geodata, poy, and the
rest) is vendored, mostly unchanged, from:

    GeoINT  (c) 2026 GeoInt contributors
    https://github.com/marouane53/GeoINT       (MIT License)

The GeoWeb additions to the engine are: the browser console (web/), the video
frame sampler (video/), Docker and docs (this repository).

ML models and datasets invoked by the engine
--------------------------------------------
The prior step runs two learned geolocation models whose licences are their
own, and which must be checked before commercial use:

  * StreetCLIP (geolocal/StreetCLIP) — CLIP ViT-L/14-336 weights trained for
    geolocation. CC-BY-NC 4.0, research only.
  * GeoCLIP — MIT.
  * GeoNames gazetteer data used for country/region/place lookups — CC-BY 4.0.

Reverse image search is performed live against public engines (Yandex, Baidu)
by the intake step; rate limits and terms of service of those services apply.

Browser assets
--------------
  * Leaflet 1.9.4 — vendored under web/static/vendor/leaflet, BSD-2-Clause.
  * OpenStreetMap tiles are loaded from tile.openstreetmap.org when the
    "OSM streets" basemap is used; the prior snapshot bases map works offline.

